{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c1","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance: Annual General Adjustment (65% of CPI, capped at 5% by Measure BB)","requirement":"Landlords of fully covered units may raise rent ceilings each year only by the Annual General Adjustment (AGA), which the Rent Board sets at 65% of the Bay Area CPI increase over the July 1 to June 30 period. Measure BB caps the AGA at 5%, and the 2026 AGA (Regulation 1148) is 1.0%, applied to 2025 permanent rent ceilings no earlier than January 1, 2026.","key_value":"AGA = 65% of CPI increase, maximum 5%; 2026 AGA: 1.0%","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Municipal Code § 13.76.110(A); Berkeley Rent Ordinance as amended by Measure BB (November 2024); Rent Board Regulation 1148","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units with a rent ceiling: most units in multifamily properties built before 1980, single-family homes with current tenancies that began before 1996, and single-family homes with five or more rooms rented individually under separate leases. Government-owned or government-subsidized units are fully or partially covered and must be registered with the Rent Board. Landlords must meet the eligibility conditions in Regulation 1148 and give tenants the required notice. Landlords with banked (unused) AGAs from prior years may raise rent above 5% to reach the rent ceiling. Partially covered units have no rent ceiling. These include new construction with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980, most other single-family homes and most condominiums.","exemptions":"The 2026 AGA does not adjust the rents of tenancies that began on or after January 1, 2025 with rents set under the Costa-Hawkins Rental Housing Act. Units where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath with the landlord are exempt only if the landlord lived on the property at the start of the tenancy. Section 202, Section 811 and HUD-insured or HUD-held projects are only partially covered because federal or state law prohibits rent control.","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[{"id":"c3","reason":"Describes which units the ordinance covers and which must register. It states no rent increase cap, formula or amount, so it is not a rent_increase_limits rule. Its coverage details are consistent with c1."}]}
